Subject: importlib: do not wait on an initializing parent package while holding the submodule lock
Origin: other, https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-agent/pull/58597
Base-Tree: tarball https://www.python.org/ftp/python/3.13.18/Python-3.13.18.tar.xz sha256:abb0102e6d4ae027509bcb82327d9dd85515b44a3ba8ad538cfc5e9847029f68

The 3.13 backport of gh-130094 (https://github.com/python/cpython/pull/155915,
commit https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/b0a181d8fcf691f4d9eaabc6d39de1eefc863272),
first released in 3.13.16, makes _find_and_load_unlocked() import a parent
package that is still initializing while it holds the submodule's module lock.
When one thread runs pkg/__init__.py and that file imports pkg.sub, while a
second thread imports pkg.sub, each thread waits for the other's lock and
importlib raises _DeadlockError. This removes that block and restores the
3.13.15 behavior. The rest of the backport, the copy of sys.meta_path, stays.
Reported upstream as https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/160045. The patch
is the one the Datadog Agent applies to its embedded CPython 3.13.17.

Verify: test tests/python_test.go::TestConcurrentPackageImport
Drop-When: never: CPython 3.13 takes only security changes now and its maintainers have not changed this block; re-check if a 3.13 release changes _find_and_load_unlocked()

diff --git a/Lib/importlib/_bootstrap.py b/Lib/importlib/_bootstrap.py
--- a/Lib/importlib/_bootstrap.py
+++ b/Lib/importlib/_bootstrap.py
@@ -1321,12 +1321,6 @@
             msg = f'{_ERR_MSG_PREFIX}{name!r}; {parent!r} is not a package'
             raise ModuleNotFoundError(msg, name=name) from None
         parent_spec = parent_module.__spec__
-        if getattr(parent_spec, '_initializing', False):
-            _call_with_frames_removed(import_, parent)
-        # Crazy side-effects (again)!
-        module = sys.modules.get(name)
-        if module is not None:
-            return module
         child = name.rpartition('.')[2]
     spec = _find_spec(name, path)
     if spec is None:
